{"name":"Kiln Dried","hex":"#a89887","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kiln","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oven or furnace or a heated chamber, for the purpose of hardening, burning, calcining or drying anything; for example, firing ceramics, curing or preserving tobacco, or drying grain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bake in a kiln; to fire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiln"},{"term":"dried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without water or moisture, said of something that has previously been wet or moist; resulting from the process of drying.","Usually of foods: cured, preserved by drying."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dried"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiln","blocks":[{"text":"A kiln is a thermally insulated chamber, a type of oven, that produces temperatures sufficient to complete some process, such as hardening, drying, or chemical changes. Kilns have been used for millennia to turn objects made from clay into pottery, tiles and bricks. Various industries use rotary kilns for pyroprocessing and to transform many other materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG/330px-Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiln","wikidata":"Q1724341"},{"title":"Drying","blocks":[{"text":"Drying is a mass transfer process consisting of the removal of water or another solvent by evaporation from a solid, semi-solid or liquid. This process is often used as a final production step before selling or packaging products. To be considered \"dried\", the final product must be solid, in the form of a continuous sheet, long pieces, particles or powder. A source of heat and an agent to remove the vapor produced by the process are often involved. In bioproducts like food, grains, and pharmaceuticals like vaccines, the solvent to be removed is almost invariably water. Desiccation may be synonymous with drying or considered an extreme form of drying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg/330px-Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drying","wikidata":"Q278061"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Indian_brick_kiln.jpg/500px-Indian_brick_kiln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Indian_brick_kiln.jpg/1280px-Indian_brick_kiln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Indian_brick_kiln.jpg/500px-Indian_brick_kiln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indian brick kiln","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndian_brick_kiln.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Hop_kiln.png/500px-Hop_kiln.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Hop_kiln.png/500px-Hop_kiln.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hops kiln","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHop_kiln.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Farnham_Pottery%2C_Wrecclesham_-_bottle_kiln.jpg/500px-Farnham_Pottery%2C_Wrecclesham_-_bottle_kiln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Farnham_Pottery%2C_Wrecclesham_-_bottle_kiln.jpg/500px-Farnham_Pottery%2C_Wrecclesham_-_bottle_kiln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut